WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.549
Welcome to Touchline.

00:00:01.549 --> 00:00:12.478
In the next few minutes, you will learn every control you need to set up a rotation, run a session, change plans on the sideline, and review the final match report.

00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:18.236
Start on the selection screen and choose two, three, four, or five teams.

00:00:18.236 --> 00:00:21.363
Every team count is included and unlimited.

00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:27.543
Each card also shows that team count’s saved colours, game time, and changeover time.

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:31.278
Open Settings at the bottom of the selection screen.

00:00:31.278 --> 00:00:34.437
Defaults are saved separately for each team count.

00:00:34.437 --> 00:00:40.628
On the Game tab, choose five unique colours; smaller sessions use the first colours in that order.

00:00:40.628 --> 00:00:45.113
Set game and changeover durations from one second to twenty-four hours.

00:00:45.113 --> 00:00:48.524
You can also enable the five-second opening countdown.

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:51.683
Save Defaults stores these choices on this device.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:55.093
The Session tab can set an end time for today.

00:00:55.093 --> 00:01:00.692
Hard Stop ends exactly on time and may shorten the final game if it meets your minimum.

00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:05.133
Finish Last Game allows a game started before the deadline to finish.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.608
Full Games Only starts only games that fit completely.

00:01:08.608 --> 00:01:11.504
Disable the end time for continuous rotation.

00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:15.996
On the Audio tab, the master switch controls timer sounds.

00:01:15.996 --> 00:01:28.886
Then enable or disable each cue: kickoff whistle, one-minute, thirty-second, and ten-second warnings, the full-time whistle, the five-to-one countdown, team callouts, and stadium crowd.

00:01:28.886 --> 00:01:31.534
Tap Test beside any cue to preview it.

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:38.084
On supported phones, Touchline briefly ducks other audio so important announcements are clear.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:42.782
After choosing teams, the match board shows Now Playing and Up Next.

00:01:42.782 --> 00:01:47.217
Start begins the optional timer; the same button pauses and resumes it.

00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:51.777
Minus or plus thirty seconds adjusts only the current game or changeover.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:57.336
Restart Game restores the full game time and pauses, which is useful after a false start.

00:01:57.336 --> 00:02:02.084
The timer moves automatically through the changeover and into the next game.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.258
Tap Maximize for the largest possible clock.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:10.953
The current teams stay above the timer, while Up Next remains visible in a compact position.

00:02:10.953 --> 00:02:14.172
Tap the same icon again to return to the full board.

00:02:14.172 --> 00:02:19.744
Keep Screen Awake helps prevent the display from sleeping while Touchline remains visible.

00:02:20.194 --> 00:02:26.648
Tap the Up Next card to jump there immediately, or open the list icon to see all upcoming games.

00:02:26.648 --> 00:02:34.447
The list includes every game that can start before the session end time; continuous sessions show one full rotation.

00:02:34.447 --> 00:02:36.867
Tap any listed game to play it next.

00:02:36.867 --> 00:02:41.909
Previous and Next also move manually, reset the timer, and leave it paused.

00:02:42.359 --> 00:02:51.129
Session Timing changes game length, changeover length, the end time, finish rule, and minimum shortened game while play is underway.

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:55.913
These are session-only changes, so your saved defaults remain untouched.

00:02:55.913 --> 00:03:01.760
The current phase keeps its remaining time, and new durations begin with the next phase.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:07.014
Use minus Team or plus Team to change the roster between two and five teams.

00:03:07.014 --> 00:03:09.796
Choose the exact colour leaving or arriving.

00:03:09.796 --> 00:03:15.991
During play, the current game and changeover finish first, then Touchline begins a fresh rotation.

00:03:15.991 --> 00:03:22.059
Late arrivals do not need catch-up games, and a newly added colour applies only to this session.

00:03:22.509 --> 00:03:27.173
View Rotation and Fairness lists every matchup and explains the schedule.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:31.966
Touchline warns when a smaller rotation requires a back-to-back appearance.

00:03:31.966 --> 00:03:36.822
Complete cycles balance game counts, and every schedule loops automatically.

00:03:36.822 --> 00:03:42.380
The five-team cycle avoids consecutive appearances, including across the loop boundary.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:47.874
Tap End Session, shown with the stop icon, and confirm when play is finished.

00:03:47.874 --> 00:03:57.568
Touchline records partial game time already played, then shows total session time, average playing time, games played, and each team’s playing time.

00:03:57.568 --> 00:04:02.874
Close the report to review the board, or return to selection for another session.
